From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 3ds-d2 <3ds-d2@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:56:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] block prologue: derive the budget-expiry skip from encoding
 sizes

The BGT over the expiry path hard-coded 10 instructions (the ARMv7 sizes of
MOV32_ and MOVW). With the ARMv6 encodings the path is 16 instructions and the
branch landed inside it, exiting every block to the epilog with a garbage EIP.
---
 third_party/box86-dynarec/dynarec/dynarec_arm_pass.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/box86-dynarec/dynarec/dynarec_arm_pass.c b/third_party/box86-dynarec/dynarec/dynarec_arm_pass.c
index d70aad3..6899e5c 100755
--- a/third_party/box86-dynarec/dynarec/dynarec_arm_pass.c
+++ b/third_party/box86-dynarec/dynarec/dynarec_arm_pass.c
@@ -236,7 +236,10 @@ uintptr_t arm_pass(dynarec_arm_t* dyn, uintptr_t addr)
             j32 = dyn->budget_tail - (dyn->arm_size + 8);
             Bcond(cLE, j32);
         } else {
-            EMIT(0xCA000000 | 9);       // BGT +10 insns (skip the expiry path)
+            // BGT over the expiry path below. Its length is computed from the
+            // per-architecture sizes of MOV32_ and MOVW (ARMv7: 2+1+1+1+1+2+1+NOP
+            // = 10 insns; ARMv6: 4+2+1+2+1+4+1+NOP = 16), so it cannot drift.
+            EMIT(0xCA000000 | (2*ARM_MOV32F_WORDS + 2*ARM_MOVW_WORDS + 4 - 1));
             // arm_epilog's stm writes emu->ip FROM THE xEIP REGISTER (stale at
             // block entry) — so load the resume address into xEIP, not memory.
             // C10 (deep review): MOV32 is VARIABLE length — 1 insn when ~imm32
